      </section>
      <h2 id="oadp-using-enable-api-group-versions_oadp-different-kubernetes-api-versions" class="group scroll-mt-20">Using Enable API Group Versions<a href="#oadp-using-enable-api-group-versions_oadp-different-kubernetes-api-versions" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Configure the <code>EnableAPIGroupVersions</code> feature flag to back up all Kubernetes API group versions that are supported on a cluster, not only the preferred one. This helps you maintain compatibility across different API groups in your cluster.</p>
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Enable API Group Versions is still in beta.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
